1. A smart lighting system for rendering a lighting scene in a room, the smart lighting system comprising:  

a plurality of luminaires disposed at respective positions in the room, each luminaire of the plurality of luminaires comprising one or more light sources configured to emit illumination into the room;  

a plurality of location sensors associated with the plurality of luminaires, the plurality of location sensors being configured to generate location information indicative of respective locations of at least two luminaires of the plurality of luminaires within the room;  

at least one sensing element configured to generate luminaire-characterization information comprising at least one of:  
(i) orientation information indicative of an orientation of at least one luminaire of the plurality of luminaires relative to the room, and  
(ii) luminaire-type information indicative of a type or optical emission characteristic of at least one luminaire of the plurality of luminaires; and  

a controller communicatively coupled to the plurality of luminaires, the plurality of location sensors, and the at least one sensing element, the controller being configured to:  

determine, based at least in part on the location information, a spatial arrangement of the plurality of luminaires in the room;  

determine, based at least in part on the luminaire-characterization information, at least one illumination capability or emission direction associated with at least one of the plurality of luminaires;  

establish a coordinate relationship between the spatial arrangement of the plurality of luminaires and a fixed reference point in the room; and  

control respective light output settings of the plurality of luminaires to render a lighting scene defined relative to the fixed reference point, such that the lighting scene is maintained with respect to the fixed reference point based on the determined spatial arrangement and the luminaire-characterization information.

1. A lighting system comprising:  

a plurality of light sources, each light source being configured to emit illumination and to determine or provide information indicative of a location of the respective light source within an environment; and  

a controller communicatively coupled to the plurality of light sources, the controller being configured to:  

receive location information associated with the plurality of light sources;  

receive scene data defining an intended illumination scene including at least one illumination effect and an intended spatial location at which the at least one illumination effect is to appear;  

determine, based at least in part on the received location information, where illumination produced by one or more of the plurality of light sources will appear in the environment;  

compare the determined appearance of the illumination with the intended spatial location of the at least one illumination effect; and  

generate adapted control commands for at least one of the plurality of light sources to cause the at least one illumination effect to appear at or substantially near the intended spatial location, thereby preserving the intended illumination scene notwithstanding a change in position, orientation, replacement, addition, or removal of one or more of the plurality of light sources.

1. **A lighting system comprising:**

   a plurality of lamps arranged in a room, each lamp comprising a controllable light source and a controller;

   wherein each of the plurality of lamps is associated with location information indicating a position of the respective lamp relative to a reference point of the room;

   wherein at least a subset of the plurality of lamps is further associated with supplemental lamp information comprising at least one of an orientation of the respective lamp and a luminaire type of the respective lamp; and

   a lighting control system configured to receive the location information and the supplemental lamp information and to generate control signals for the plurality of lamps based on the location information and, for the subset of lamps, the supplemental lamp information;

   wherein the control signals cause the plurality of lamps to render a lighting effect in the room such that spatial characteristics of the lighting effect are adjusted according to the respective positions of the lamps relative to the reference point and according to at least one of the orientations and luminaire types of the subset of lamps.
